# musingnotes.app — Marketing Site

Static marketing site for **Musing**, a context-aware on-device notes app. Plain HTML/CSS/JS: **no build step, no framework, no npm dependencies.** Everything served is a file in `public/`.

## Sibling Repos

| Repo | Path | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| **This site** | `~/Cursor/musingnotes-site` | musingnotes.app |
| **iOS app** | `~/Cursor/AmbientNotes` | iPhone + Watch + widgets |
| **Mac app** | `~/Cursor/Musing-Mac` | Native macOS (worktree of the iOS repo, branch `mac-app`) |

The app repos are the source of truth for design tokens and privacy claims. When site copy and app behavior disagree, **the app wins** — fix the site.

## Layout

```
public/
├── index.html          landing page
├── privacy.html        the App Store privacy URL — /privacy.html
├── styles.css          all styles + five-room theme tokens
├── theme.js            theme picker, shelf render, localStorage
├── blog/               index.html + one .html per post
├── mockups/            design explorations, not linked from the live site
├── shot-*.jpg          app screenshots used in sections
├── icon.png            favicon + apple-touch-icon
├── og-card.png         social preview, exactly 1200×630
├── sitemap.xml, robots.txt
└── (repo root) wrangler.toml — [assets] directory = "./public"
```

## Deploy

Cloudflare Workers Builds is connected to this repo. **Pushing to `main` auto-deploys** — Cloudflare runs `npx wrangler deploy`, which reads `wrangler.toml` and publishes `public/`. There is no manual upload and no staging environment, so `main` is production.

To change the site: edit a file in `public/`, commit, push to `main`.

## Key Facts

- **App Store:** `https://apps.apple.com/us/app/musing-notes/id6777539170`
- **Support:** support@musingnotes.app
- **Font:** Inter via Google Fonts — preconnect both `fonts.googleapis.com` and `fonts.gstatic.com`
- Blog URLs are **extensionless** in links and `sitemap.xml` (`/blog/why-folders-kill-your-ideas`) while the files are `.html`. Cloudflare's asset handler resolves this — don't "fix" the links by adding `.html`.
